WEBVTT

00:00.510 --> 00:02.640
Let's say that I'm
working in a restaurant,

00:02.640 --> 00:04.870
and I'm making $10 per hour.

00:04.870 --> 00:09.670
But on top of my hourly wage,
I also get tips each hour.

00:09.670 --> 00:12.120
So this entire expression,
you can view this

00:12.120 --> 00:15.630
as how much I might
make in a given hour.

00:15.630 --> 00:18.580
Now, you might also realize
that the number of tips

00:18.580 --> 00:20.470
or the amount of tips
I might make in an hour

00:20.470 --> 00:23.040
can change dramatically
from hour to hour.

00:23.040 --> 00:26.120
It can vary-- one hour it
might be lunchtime, get

00:26.120 --> 00:28.530
a lot of tips, people might
get some big-ticket items.

00:28.530 --> 00:30.480
The next hour, I might
not have any customers.

00:30.480 --> 00:32.740
And then my tips
might be really low.

00:32.740 --> 00:35.010
So the tips part
right over here,

00:35.010 --> 00:37.730
we consider that--
the entire word,

00:37.730 --> 00:40.370
we consider that
to be a variable.

00:40.370 --> 00:43.100
From scenario to
scenario, it can change.

00:43.100 --> 00:47.340
So for example, in one
scenario, maybe it's lunchtime.

00:47.340 --> 00:49.130
I'm getting really big tips.

00:49.130 --> 00:53.350
So tips is-- let's
say it's equal to $30.

00:53.350 --> 00:56.470
And so the total amount I
might make in that hour--

00:56.470 --> 00:58.730
we can go back to this
expression right over here--

00:58.730 --> 01:02.360
it's going to be 10 plus--
instead of writing tips here,

01:02.360 --> 01:06.730
I'll write 30 because that's
what my tips are in that hour.

01:06.730 --> 01:10.590
And so that is going
to be equal to 40.

01:10.590 --> 01:12.810
Let me do it in
that yellow color.

01:12.810 --> 01:15.820
It's going to be equal to $40.

01:15.820 --> 01:18.860
But let's say right after that,
the restaurant slows down.

01:18.860 --> 01:20.860
We're out of the lunch
hour for whatever reason.

01:20.860 --> 01:23.970
Maybe the restaurant next door
has a big sale or something.

01:23.970 --> 01:26.910
And so the next hour, my
tips go down dramatically.

01:26.910 --> 01:30.640
My tips go down to
$5 for that hour.

01:30.640 --> 01:32.870
Now I go back to
this expression.

01:32.870 --> 01:35.190
The total I make
is my hourly wage

01:35.190 --> 01:42.720
plus the $5 in tips,
which is equal to $15.

01:42.720 --> 01:45.920
As you see, this entire
expression-- the 10 plus tips--

01:45.920 --> 01:51.170
it changed depending on what the
value of the variable tips is.

01:51.170 --> 01:54.180
Now, you won't see whole
words typically used

01:54.180 --> 01:56.020
in algebra as variables.

01:56.020 --> 01:56.900
We get lazy.

01:56.900 --> 02:00.040
And so instead, we tend to use
just easier-to-write symbols.

02:00.040 --> 02:02.520
And so in this context,
instead of writing tips,

02:02.520 --> 02:08.009
maybe we could have
just written 10 plus t,

02:08.009 --> 02:10.424
where t represents the tips
that we get in an hour.

02:10.424 --> 02:11.840
And so then we
would say, OK, what

02:11.840 --> 02:13.310
happens when t is equal to 30?

02:19.040 --> 02:20.500
Well, then, we have a situation.

02:20.500 --> 02:21.950
t is equal to 30.

02:21.950 --> 02:25.830
This evaluates to 10 plus
30, which would be 40.

02:25.830 --> 02:28.500
What would happen
if t is equal to 5?

02:28.500 --> 02:31.660
Well, then, this would
evaluate to 10 plus 5,

02:31.660 --> 02:34.810
which is equal to 15.

02:34.810 --> 02:35.840
Now, I want to be clear.

02:35.840 --> 02:37.090
We didn't even have to use t.

02:37.090 --> 02:38.881
We didn't even really
have to use a letter,

02:38.881 --> 02:41.420
although in traditional algebra,
you almost do use a letter.

02:41.420 --> 02:46.220
We could have written
it as 10 plus x, where

02:46.220 --> 02:49.590
x is your tips per hour.
x might not be as natural.

02:49.590 --> 02:51.670
It's not the first
letter in the word tips.

02:51.670 --> 02:57.200
Or you could have even
written 10 plus star,

02:57.200 --> 02:58.960
where you could
say star represents

02:58.960 --> 03:00.270
the number of tips in an hour.

03:00.270 --> 03:02.609
But it just might have not
made as much intuitive sense.

03:02.609 --> 03:04.400
But hopefully this
gives you a general idea

03:04.400 --> 03:07.790
of just what a variable is.

03:07.790 --> 03:13.610
All it is is a symbol that
represents varying values.

03:13.610 --> 03:16.410
And that's why we
call it a variable.
